<!--
================================================================================
  Sample putEvent message for NEHR submission
  Project:    NEHR Onboarding — Heart Clinic / MDXcess GCMS
  Spec ref:   putEvent_v0.2_20251224.xlsx (Synapxe), Request tab
  Generated:  2026-05-04 (illustrative — element ordering follows the spec)

  This is a CLINICAL message (msgType = Clinical) for an outpatient cardiology
  visit. It uses dummy patient data drawn from the Heart Clinic GCMS backup,
  populated to illustrate what each XML element should contain and where the
  GCMS source value lives. See NEHR_putEvent_Mapping_Analysis_2026-05-04.xlsx
  for the full per-field mapping.

  COLOUR-CODE OF FIELDS (for the developer):
    [HARDCODE]  fixed value baked into the NEHR Adapter
    [GCMS]      pulled from a GCMS table.column at runtime
    [DERIVE]    computed at runtime (e.g. concatenate, lookup, format)
    [TRANSLATE] GCMS value mapped through a translation table to NHDD code
    [GAP]       column does not yet exist — placeholder shown
    [N/A]       not applicable for outpatient — DO NOT SEND
================================================================================
-->
<putEvent xmlns="http://www.synapxe.sg/nehr/putEvent">
  <!-- ========================================================== -->
  <!-- CONTROL HEADER — generated by the NEHR Adapter on every send -->
  <!-- ========================================================== -->
  <controlHeader>
    <!-- HCI code of the institution. Heart Clinic main = 9403258. -->
    <!-- [HARDCODE] / [DERIVE] from Tbl_PatientAppointment.Branch (22 = main, 26 = Farrer) -->
    <!-- TODO: confirm Farrer HCI code (Q9 in Client Questions sheet) -->
    <srcInstitution>9403258</srcInstitution>
    <!-- Full HSCA Licensee number (NEW field per Guide v0.42). [HARDCODE] -->
    <licenseeNumber>L/9403258/MDS/007/242</licenseeNumber>
    <!-- Identifies the source software, NOT the clinic. [HARDCODE] -->
    <srcApplication>MDX-GCMS</srcApplication>
    <!-- Unique message identifier per send. [DERIVE] — generate UUID at adapter -->
    <msgID>MDX-GCMS-EVT-20260504-00001</msgID>
    <!-- Sequence number, increments per message per data type per source. [DERIVE] -->
    <msgSequenceID>1</msgSequenceID>
    <!-- ISO 8601 datetime WITH +08:00 timezone (required for A&A validation). [DERIVE] -->
    <msgDateTime>2026-05-04T18:30:00+08:00</msgDateTime>
    <!-- Message mode. Values: Clinical | Administrative | Cancel | Merge -->
    <!-- "Clinical" = create/update an actualized visit (this example) -->
    <msgType>Clinical</msgType>
  </controlHeader>
  <!-- ========================================================== -->
  <!-- PATIENT — demographics + identification                      -->
  <!-- ========================================================== -->
  <patient>
    <identification>
      <!-- Patient document ID, uppercase. [GCMS] Tbl_PatientParticular.Patient_NRIC -->
      <id>S8743573C</id>
      <!-- Source MRN — must be unique non-editable. Prefix with srcApplication. -->
      <!-- [TRANSLATE] "MDX-GCMS^" + Tbl_PatientParticular.Reg_No -->
      <MRNNumber>MDX-GCMS^13005116</MRNNumber>
      <!-- NHDD ID type code. SP=Pink IC, SB=Blue IC, SH=Birth Cert, SO=FIN, FP=Foreign Passport, MP=Malaysian Passport, NA=Not Applicable -->
      <!-- [DERIVE] from Patient_NRIC pattern + a NEW UI field (currently SP/SB/SH cannot be distinguished from NRIC alone) -->
      <type>SP</type>
      <!-- Only populated during patient-merge messages (msgType=Merge). Omitted here. -->
      <!-- <patientMergeType>...</patientMergeType> -->
    </identification>
    <name>
      <!-- Full name as printed on identification document. [TRANSLATE] FirstName + " " + SurName -->
      <value>THALVINDERPAL SINGH SANDHU</value>
      <!-- NHDD title code. [TRANSLATE] Tbl_PatientParticular.Salutation ("Mr." → MR) -->
      <title>MR</title>
    </name>
    <!-- Patient alias name (optional). For names like "LIM SOO SUAT @ CHEN SOON FA". -->
    <!-- [CONFIRM] possibly Tbl_PatientParticular.OtherName — pending client confirmation -->
    <!-- <aliasName>
           <value>...</value>
           <title>...</title>
         </aliasName> -->
    <contactDetails>
      <address>
        <!-- NHDD address-type code (Home, Office, etc.). Hardcode "Home" for typical case. -->
        <type>Home</type>
        <!-- [CONFIRM] patient address columns NOT visible in Tbl_PatientParticular - blocked by Q1 -->
        <!-- Likely future mapping (parallel to Tbl_Patient_NextOfKin schema): -->
        <streetLine1>BLK 123 #05-67</streetLine1>
        <streetLine2>HOUGANG AVENUE 8</streetLine2>
        <city>SINGAPORE</city>
        <country>SG</country>
        <!-- [TRANSLATE] Tbl_Country → ISO code -->
        <postalCode>530123</postalCode>
      </address>
      <phone>
        <!-- NHDD phone type. M=Mobile, H=Home, O=Office. -->
        <type>M</type>
        <!-- [HARDCODE] for Singapore mobiles. -->
        <countryCode>65</countryCode>
        <!-- areaCode and extensionNumber typically omitted for Singapore mobiles. -->
        <!-- [CONFIRM] Tbl_PatientParticular.Mobile_No OR Tbl_Patient_PhoneNo.Patient_PhoneNo - blocked by Q2 -->
        <phoneNumber>91234567</phoneNumber>
      </phone>
    </contactDetails>
    <!-- DOB in ISO date format. [TRANSLATE] from YYYYMMDD string to YYYY-MM-DD -->
    <dateOfBirth>1987-12-27</dateOfBirth>
    <!-- Optional NHDD-coded. [GAP] — not captured in GCMS. Omit or add column later. -->
    <!-- <countryOfBirth>SG</countryOfBirth> -->
    <!-- NHDD gender. M=Male, F=Female, U=Unknown. [TRANSLATE] "Male" → M -->
    <gender>M</gender>
    <!-- Email. [GCMS] Tbl_PatientParticular.Email -->
    <emailAddress>thalvinder.singh@example.com</emailAddress>
    <!-- NHDD nationality. [TRANSLATE] Tbl_Nationality.Nationality_ID → NHDD code. -->
    <nationality>SG</nationality>
    <!-- ********** RACE — MANDATORY but currently a SCHEMA GAP ********** -->
    <!-- [GAP] No Race column in Tbl_PatientParticular and no Tbl_Race lookup. -->
    <!-- Developer must add a Race column + lookup + UI dropdown before any putEvent will validate. -->
    <!-- Placeholder shown to illustrate the expected XML; real values to come from new lookup. -->
    <race>CN</race>
    <!-- e.g. CN=Chinese, MY=Malay, IN=Indian, EU=Eurasian, OT=Others -->
    <!-- Optional NHDD-coded. [GAP] - defer for Phase 1. -->
    <!-- <residencyStatus>...</residencyStatus> -->
    <!-- NHDD language. [TRANSLATE] Tbl_PatientParticular.Language (split comma-separated, take first) -->
    <language>EN</language>
    <!-- NHDD marital status: A=Separated, D=Divorced, M=Married, S=Single, U=Unknown, W=Widowed -->
    <!-- [TRANSLATE] Tbl_PatientParticular.Martial_Status ("Single" → S; "Select" → omit) -->
    <maritalStatus>S</maritalStatus>
    <!-- NHDD occupation code. [TRANSLATE] Tbl_PatientParticular.Occupation_ID → NHDD. -->
    <!-- Skip rows 1-6 in Tbl_Occupation (lookup contamination). -->
    <occupation>OT-CLERK</occupation>
    <!-- ===== DO NOT SEND — NEHR sources these from MHA per Guide page 14 ===== -->
    <!-- <VIPFlag>...</VIPFlag>           [N/A] -->
    <!-- <VVIPFlag>...</VVIPFlag>         [N/A] -->
    <!-- <dateOfDeath>...</dateOfDeath>   [N/A] -->
    <!-- <deathIndicator>...</deathIndicator> [N/A] -->
    <!-- Optional NHDD-coded. [GAP] - defer for Phase 1. -->
    <!-- <religion>...</religion> -->
    <nextOfKin>
      <!-- [TRANSLATE] Tbl_Patient_NextOfKin.FirstName + SurName -->
      <name>SANDHU GURMIT KAUR</name>
      <!-- [TRANSLATE] pick first non-null among MobileNumber / HomeNumber / OfficeNumber -->
      <phone>98765432</phone>
      <!-- [GAP] no Relationship column in Tbl_Patient_NextOfKin. Developer to add. -->
      <relationship>SP</relationship>
      <!-- SP=Spouse, PR=Parent, CH=Child, etc. -->
      <!-- [GCMS] Tbl_Patient_NextOfKin.Email -->
      <email>gurmit.k@example.com</email>
    </nextOfKin>
  </patient>
  <!-- ========================================================== -->
  <!-- EVENT — the actual visit (omitted for Administrative/Cancel) -->
  <!-- ========================================================== -->
  <event>
    <!-- Stable across amendments and cancellations. [GCMS] Tbl_PatientAppointment.Auto_AppointmentID -->
    <recordIdentifier>bc1de036-0af1-4170-99c0-2907e26cf75422</recordIdentifier>
    <!-- The case/visit number. Used as eventID to tie clinical data to this visit. -->
    <!-- [GCMS] Tbl_PatientAppointment.Appointment_ID -->
    <id>000583cd-4522-4c40-8724-62762d6a7f15</id>
    <!-- Always 1 for outpatient. [HARDCODE] -->
    <movementSequenceNo>1</movementSequenceNo>
    <!-- ISO datetime with timezone. [DERIVE] Appointment_Start_Date + " " + App_Start_Time → ISO -->
    <eventStartDate>2026-05-04T15:30:00+08:00</eventStartDate>
    <!-- When the patient leaves clinic with no further updates. NOT bill finalisation. -->
    <!-- [DERIVE] Appointment_End_Date + " " + App_End_Time → ISO -->
    <eventEndDate>2026-05-04T16:00:00+08:00</eventEndDate>
    <!-- false for new/update; true ONLY for cancellation messages. [DERIVE] -->
    <cancellationNotice>false</cancellationNotice>
    <!-- HCI code of the institution serving this visit. [TRANSLATE] from Branch FK. -->
    <institution>9403258</institution>
    <!-- Doctor's specialty. [HARDCODE] "Cardiology" for Heart Clinic. -->
    <!-- Codeset source: NEHR Codeset Inventory v2.29, sheet "Service Speciality", row 4. -->
    <serviceSpecialty>
      <code>NEHR_SS_0002</code>
      <codingSchemeName>Service_Specialty_(NEHR)</codingSchemeName>
      <!-- codingSchemeVersion typically omitted -->
      <textDescription>Cardiology</textDescription>
    </serviceSpecialty>
    <!-- O = Outpatient. ALWAYS for Heart Clinic. [HARDCODE] -->
    <!-- Codeset source: NEHR Codeset Inventory v2.29, sheet "Patient Type". Full codeset: O=Outpatient, I=Inpatient. -->
    <patientType>
      <code>O</code>
      <codingSchemeName>Patient_Type_(NEHR)</codingSchemeName>
      <textDescription>Outpatient</textDescription>
    </patientType>
    <!-- 4 = Outpatient Visit. ALWAYS for Heart Clinic. [HARDCODE] -->
    <!-- Codeset source: NEHR Codeset Inventory v2.29, sheet "Event Type". Full codeset: 1=Admission, 2=Discharge, 4=Outpatient Visit. -->
    <eventType>
      <code>4</code>
      <!-- codes (1=Admission, 2=Discharge, 4=Outpatient Visit) -->
      <codingSchemeName>Movement_Category_(NEHR)</codingSchemeName>
      <textDescription>Outpatient Visit</textDescription>
    </eventType>
    <!-- 1 = Primary Care Visit. ALWAYS for Heart Clinic outpatient. [HARDCODE] -->
    <!-- Codeset source: NEHR Codeset Inventory v2.29, sheet "Movement Type" (codes: 1=Primary Care Visit, 2=Emergency Visit). -->
    <!-- Note: in v0.2 spec, movementType is OPTIONAL — populating it for clarity per Guide narrative. -->
    <movementType>
      <code>1</code>
      <!-- codes (1=Primary Care Visit, 2=Emergency Visit) -->
      <codingSchemeName>Visit_Type_(NEHR)</codingSchemeName>
      <textDescription>Primary Care Visit</textDescription>
    </movementType>
    <!-- The doctor who saw the patient. -->
    <!-- [TRANSLATE] Tbl_PatientAppointment.Resource_ID → Tbl_ResourceWithNRIC (filter Doctor) → Tbl_Doctor -->
    <attendingClinician>
      <!-- MCR number. [GCMS] Tbl_Doctor.RegNo via the resource chain. -->
      <id>04173D</id>
      <!-- Full name. [TRANSLATE] Tbl_Doctor.First_Name + " " + Sur_Name. -->
      <name>Ruth Kam</name>
    </attendingClinician>
    <!-- ========== INPATIENT-ONLY — DO NOT SEND for outpatient cardiology ========== -->
    <!-- <admittingClinician>...</admittingClinician>     [N/A] -->
    <!-- <dischargingClinician>...</dischargingClinician> [N/A] -->
    <!-- <dischargeInformation>...</dischargeInformation> [N/A] -->
    <!-- Optional. Send only if the visit was via referral and the referring doctor's MCR is known. -->
    <!-- [CONFIRM] Tbl_PatientParticular.ReferredBy is free text — needs MCR enrichment (Q12) -->
    <!--
    <referringClinician>
      <id>M12345A</id>
      <name>DR JOHN TAN</name>
    </referringClinician>
    -->
  </event>
</putEvent>
<!--
================================================================================
  HOW TO USE THIS SAMPLE
================================================================================

  1. The XML structure here matches the element order in
     putEvent_v0.2_20251224.xlsx > Request tab.
     Ordering matters for XSD validation.

  2. Every value above is illustrative. The NEHR Adapter must populate from:
     - GCMS database (Tbl_PatientAppointment, Tbl_PatientParticular, Tbl_Doctor,
       Tbl_ResourceWithNRIC, Tbl_Patient_NextOfKin, lookup tables)
     - Hardcoded values (srcApplication, licenseeNumber, the fixed-value codings
       for outpatient: O / 4 / 1)
     - Derived values (msgID, msgDateTime, ID type, ISO datetime concatenation)
     - Translation maps (gender Male→M, marital "Single"→S, language→NHDD,
       country→ISO, etc. — see Sheet 4 of the Mapping Analysis workbook)

  3. Validate every generated message against the XSDs (typeDef.xsd +
     putEvent_Request.xsd) BEFORE transmission. Per Guide page 18: messages
     failing XSD validation must not be sent.

  4. Key rules to enforce in adapter logic:
     a. Source must EXCLUDE empty XML tags. Never emit <tag/> or <tag></tag>
        for unmapped fields. Skip the element entirely.
     b. Patient ID must NOT appear in any element other than identification.id.
     c. recordIdentifier must remain stable across creation → amendment →
        cancellation. Same recordIdentifier, new state.
     d. Trigger: Tbl_PatientAppointment.Status = 'finished' → send Clinical.
        Status = 'appointment' (not yet seen) → do not send.
     e. msgID + msgSequenceID + (srcInstitution + srcApplication + msgDateTime)
        must be unique per message. Duplicate → NEHR rejects.

  5. Variations of this message:
     - Administrative (demographics update, no event):
       Same controlHeader + patient. No <event> segment. msgType=Administrative.
     - Cancel (deactivate patient master after wrong registration):
       Same controlHeader + patient. No <event> segment. msgType=Cancel.
     - Merge (link two patient masters):
       controlHeader + patient WITH identification.patientMergeType populated.
       msgType=Merge.
     - Cancel a visit (e.g. patient no-show after data was already sent):
       Same as Clinical, but event.cancellationNotice=true. Cancel all clinical
       data first, then cancel the visit.

  6. Open items still preventing a real submission (see Client Questions sheet):
     - Race column does not exist in GCMS (CRITICAL)
     - Patient address storage location unconfirmed (Q1)
     - Patient phone storage location unconfirmed (Q2)
     - Farrer branch HCI code unconfirmed (Q9)
     - Visit lifecycle confirmation (Q8)

================================================================================
-->